0 -16 Td (Page 1: Introduction to Artificial Intelligence) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) is a multidisciplinary field of computer science focused on creating systems capable of performing tasks that typically require human intelligence. These tasks include visual perception, speech recognition, decision-making, and translation between languages. In academic environments, students and researchers must routinely process vast quantities of textual information, ranging from textbooks to research papers and lecture slides.) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (Modern advancements in Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) and Large Language Models \(LLMs\) have transformed how scholars interact with academic literature. Rather than manually scanning hundreds of pages, automated systems can extract key concepts, identify connections across topics, and answer contextual queries with precision.) Tj
ET
