0 -16 Td (Page 2: Machine Learning Paradigms & Deep Learning) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (Machine learning algorithms build mathematical models based on sample training data to make predictions or decisions without being explicitly programmed for each specific scenario. The primary learning paradigms include:) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (1. Supervised Learning: Learning a function that maps an input to an output based on example input-output pairs. Common algorithms include linear regression, support vector machines, and deep neural networks.) Tj
0 -16 Td (2. Unsupervised Learning: Discovering hidden patterns or data groupings without labeled responses. Common methods include k-means clustering and principal component analysis.) Tj
0 -16 Td (3. Reinforcement Learning: Training agents to take actions in an environment to maximize cumulative reward through trial and error.) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (Deep Learning architectures, particularly multi-layer neural networks and transformers, serve as the foundational backbone for modern document analysis systems.) Tj
ET
endstream
