(Academic Document Assistant - Research Notes) Tj
0 -16 Td (Page 3: Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) Architecture) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) addresses key limitations of static large language models, including hallucinations and outdated factual knowledge. RAG combines external knowledge retrieval with neural text generation.) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (The standard RAG pipeline operates as follows:) Tj
0 -16 Td (First, source documents are ingested and split into manageable text chunks. Next, an embedding model transforms each chunk into a dense vector representation reflecting its semantic meaning. These vectors are indexed within a high-performance vector database such as FAISS.) Tj
0 -16 Td () Tj
0 -16 Td (When a student poses a query, the query is embedded into the same vector space, and similarity search identifies the top matching chunks. Finally, the retrieved chunks along with the query are formatted into a prompt and submitted to the language model, which generates a factually grounded answer with verifiable source citations.) Tj
ET
endstream
